{"shortDescription":"By Avinash  P and Ragini MathurMost Latin American stocks and currencies rose on Tuesday, led by Brazilian and Colombian assets, as higher oil prices buoyed regional exporters despite caution over a global bond selloff.The MSCI Latin America equities index (MILA00000PUS) gained 0.9%, hitting a near…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["By Avinash  P and Ragini Mathur"]},{"type":"p","children":["Most Latin American stocks and currencies rose on Tuesday, led by Brazilian and Colombian assets, as higher oil prices buoyed regional exporters despite caution over a global bond selloff."]},{"type":"p","children":["The MSCI Latin America equities index (MILA00000PUS) gained 0.9%, hitting a near one-month high earlier in the session. Brazil's Bovespa ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"BMFBOVESPA:IBOV","text":"BMFBOVESPA:IBOV"}}," rose 1.6% and was on track for a tenth consecutive session of gains, its longest winning streak since November 2025."]},{"type":"p","children":["Petrobras ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"BMFBOVESPA:PETR3","text":"BMFBOVESPA:PETR3"}}," climbed 4%, providing the biggest lift to the Brazilian benchmark. Data showed the country's oil output rose 13.6% year-on-year in July to a record 4.5 million barrels per day."]},{"type":"p","children":["Oil prices jumped to a one-week high on Tuesday as a resumption in fighting between the U.S. and Iran renewed fears of supply disruptions from the Middle East."]},{"type":"p","children":["The surging crude prices supported oil-exporting economies in the region, which have also benefited as producers in the Americas boost exports to Asian buyers seeking alternatives to Gulf crude."]},{"type":"p","children":["Brazil's economy slowed in the second quarter as high borrowing costs weighed on activity, though growth slightly beat expectations on a strong farm sector."]},{"type":"p","children":["\"The data therefore reinforce our view that restrictive monetary policy is gradually gaining traction, rather than pointing to an abrupt downturn,\" said Andres Abadia, chief Latin America economist at Pantheon Macroeconomics."]},{"type":"p","children":["The real ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"FX_IDC:USDBRL","text":"FX_IDC:USDBRL"}}," gained 0.6%, helping lift MSCI's Latin American currency gauge (.MILA00000CUS) by 0.4%. The Colombian peso ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"FX_IDC:USDCOP","text":"FX_IDC:USDCOP"}}," rose 1.9%."]},{"type":"p","children":["Still, broader sentiment remained fragile as investors weighed the conflict's economic fallout and whether higher borrowing costs could stoke inflation. While the U.S. dollar ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"TVC:DXY","text":"TVC:DXY"}}," was firmer against some major currencies, concerns over U.S. policy credibility and government borrowing clouded its broader outlook."]},{"type":"p","children":["\"Right now, it looks like the U.S. dollar is showing a lot of underlying weakness, and meanwhile these two emerging economies seem to have potential to continue providing a very good, or a more fortunate situation,\" said Juan Perez, director of trading at Monex."]},{"type":"p","children":["Perez said that resilience could fade if U.S. policy credibility improves and fiscal concerns in Brazil and Colombia return to focus."]},{"type":"p","children":["Mexico's stock index ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"BMV:ME","text":"BMV:ME"}}," fell 1.4%, while the peso ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"FX_IDC:USDMXN","text":"FX_IDC:USDMXN"}}," was little changed. Uncertainty surrounding stalled North American free trade negotiations is deterring new investment and prompting some companies already operating in Mexico to consider alternative locations."]},{"type":"p","children":["Chile's peso ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"FX_IDC:USDCLP","text":"FX_IDC:USDCLP"}}," eased 0.2% after July economic activity contracted, dragged by a slowdown in mining."]},{"type":"p","chi